Slackware Post-Install Scripts (PIS)

'Let the Slackers be a little bit lazy. ;)' 

PIS is a dialog-based assistant for selected Slackware 15.0 post-
installation tasks. It configures locale and keyboards, login mode,
users and wheel administration, X sessions, ELILO kernels, slackpkg
mirrors and selected package-management tools.

Version 0.3.0 validates changes, displays the current configuration,
creates automatic backups and supports restoration. Its portable
profiles store mirror URLs and never contain passwords.

PIS changes standard Slackware configuration files. Backups are stored
under /var/log/PIS/backups and can be restored from the PIS menu or with
"pis --restore". The ELILO module is available only when an existing
ELILO configuration is detected.

PIS does not replace Slackware's native network and service tools.
